        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeff Martin, Kyle Patrick, Ethan\n- Organizations: The Tea Party, The Click Five\n- Products: Live at the Corner Hotel, \"Don't Let Me Go\"\n- Places: Windsor, Ontario, Atlanta, Georgia, Boston\n- Roles: guitarist, singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, producer, lead singer\n\nFacts:\n- Jeff Martin was born on October 2, 1969, in Windsor, Ontario.\n- Jeff Martin is a Canadian guitarist and singer-songwriter best known for fronting the rock band The Tea Party.\n- Kyle Patrick Dickherber was born on May 20, 1986, in Atlanta, Georgia, United States.\n- Kyle Patrick is an American singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and producer best known as the lead singer of the Boston power pop band The Click Five.\n- In October 2005, Jeff Martin began his career as a solo artist when The Tea Party went on hiatus.\n- In 2008, Live at the Corner Hotel was released as a live album by Canadian singer-songwriter Jeff Martin.\n- In 2008, Kyle and Ethan performed the song \"Don't Let Me Go\" during tours and shows, with Ethan on guitar and Kyle singing.",
